      "writtenOn": "2024-09-19T01:37:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we want a bit more granularity than just the starting alignment (256 is probably okay for SSBO/UBO but if we can extend it to vertex buffers, they only have a 4 byte alignment I believe).\n\nI\u0027d vote to just have another constant that controls allocation granularity within the `sufficient_size()` function, e.g. take `max(requiredSize, curBlockSize)` and then round to nearest 1kb. That will keep the rounding logic more consistent as the block size itself is changing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 433,
        "startChar": 59,
        "endLine": 433,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "935923560f4726d887b6ec356dd2403d859e778d",
